It embeds two public time-stamping root certificates, unmodified, as trust anchors:
DigiCert Trusted Root G4 (DigiCert Inc) and Sectigo Public Time Stamping Root R46
(Sectigo Limited). Each remains the property of its issuer; they are included only
so the verifier can check RFC 3161 time-stamp tokens offline.
